  "body_html": "<h1>Root Datum of a Reductive Group</h1>\n<p>Let \\(G\\) be a connected reductive group over an algebraically closed field,\nand let \\(T\\subseteq G\\) be a maximal torus. Write\n\\[\nX=X^*(T),\\qquad X^\\vee=X_*(T).\n\\]\nThe adjoint action of \\(T\\) on \\(\\operatorname{Lie}(G)\\) gives a finite set\nof nonzero weights \\(\\Phi\\subset X\\), called the roots. For each\n\\(\\alpha\\in\\Phi\\), the corresponding rank-one subgroup determines a coroot\n\\(\\alpha^\\vee\\in X^\\vee\\). The quadruple\n\\[\n(X,\\Phi,X^\\vee,\\Phi^\\vee)\n\\]\nis a root datum.</p>\n<p>Changing the maximal torus \\(T\\) conjugates the construction, so the\nisomorphism class of the root datum depends only on \\(G\\).</p>\n<p>The Weyl group\n\\[\nW(G,T)=N_G(T)/C_G(T)\n\\]\nacts faithfully on \\(X\\) and is generated by the reflections\n\\[\ns_\\alpha(x)=x-\\langle x,\\alpha^\\vee\\rangle\\alpha.\n\\]</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
